<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Budgie ships with the hardened runtime (required for notarization) but is
      NOT sandboxed: it types transcripts into other apps via Accessibility and
      watches the push-to-talk key via Input Monitoring, both of which the App
      Sandbox forbids. Developer ID apps don't need the sandbox, so we omit it.

      Under the hardened runtime, microphone access is gated by this entitlement
      even after the user grants the TCC prompt — without it the OS denies the
      audio tap. Accessibility and Input Monitoring are TCC permissions, not
      entitlements, and need no declaration here.

      All bundled parakeet.cpp dylibs are re-signed with the same Developer ID,
      so the default library-validation policy passes and we do NOT weaken it
      with com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
